From 899ba86ab9dc959d0df2ea2381181a00db258cef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CrockMr <118761873+CrockMr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:10:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Expose calculated health maxima in the oracle state dump

health[].maximum now carries Meitou's calculated HealthPart.MaxHp
instead of null, null when negative or non-finite as the native probe
does. It is documented as calculated, not the original's stored
_maxHealth: agreement is Observed only for unworn organic humans at
scale 1 in the setup heal receipts. The capture stays read-only; a
test pins plain, scaled, worn, stump, worn-away and non-finite parts
and checks that the state hash is unchanged. order stays null.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/oracle.md                                | 13 +++++--
 src/Meitou.Game/Oracle/OracleState.cs         |  4 +--
 tests/Meitou.Tests/Oracle/OracleStateTests.cs | 35 ++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/oracle.md b/docs/oracle.md
index 64195121..32609181 100644
--- a/docs/oracle.md
+++ b/docs/oracle.md
@@ -92,9 +92,16 @@ The additive 0.2 fields expose saved-origin evidence, broad melee/ranged combat
 mode and squad templates. Town placement/current membership/origin remain null:
 equality of native `Town::instanceID.uid` and `TownSite.InstanceId` is unproven.
 Names, array indexes, town definition IDs and transient HANDs are not substitutes.
-`order` and `health[].maximum` remain null where original-task/stored-health
-equivalence is unknown. Template fallbacks on newly created squads also need
-their own semantic verification.
+`order` remains null: a Meitou act-out row is not proof of the original
+running task. `health[].maximum` is Meitou's calculated `MaxHp` (base, or 5 for
+a stump, or the fitted prosthetic's HP, times multiplier and scale, minus wear),
+null when negative or non-finite as in the native probe. It is not the
+original's stored `_maxHealth`: the two agreed in the setup heal receipts of
+the 1 November 2026 campaign (**Observed**, unworn organic humans at scale 1,
+full health), and agreement under wear, stumps, prosthetics, robots or other
+scales is **Unknown**. Reading it changes no simulation state or state hash
+(**Verified**, `OracleStateTests`). Template fallbacks on newly created squads
+also need their own semantic verification.
 
 In Oracle mode, `--seed` is applied to the in-memory save before `SaveLoader`
 and its first draws; it replaces the save's stored seed without rewriting that
diff --git a/src/Meitou.Game/Oracle/OracleState.cs b/src/Meitou.Game/Oracle/OracleState.cs
